{"parentUuid":"6c3d5193-b337-4ed8-847e-06453504fd2d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a06de6cc1a7950537","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0118TYy6M7tdTB4zNk7YcLvY","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SAT Competition 2025 results winner main track parallel\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"The Results of SAT Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/satcomp25slides.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/\"},{\"title\":\"KIT - SAtRes - MallobSat scores 1st in SAT Competition\",\"url\":\"https://satres.kikit.kit.edu/news/2025-08-15-satcomp/\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2024\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2024/\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competitions\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2023\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2023/\"},{\"title\":\"19th International Satisﬁability Modulo Theories\",\"url\":\"https://smt-comp.github.io/2024/rules.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CanSat Competition\",\"url\":\"https://cansatcompetition.com/winners.html\"},{\"title\":\"SAT solver - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SAT_solver\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about the SAT Competition 2025 results:\n\n## Main Track Winner\n\nMallobSat scored the best on unsatisfiable instances and the 2nd best on satisfiable instances (after Painless-PRS-Kissat), overall resulting in a 1st place by a rather small margin (3% to Painless-PRS-Kissat in terms of the PAR-2 evaluation metric).\n\n## Parallel Track Information\n\nThe parallel track had a timeout of 1000s (previously 5000s) and included 8 parallel solvers.\n\nThe slides of the SAT Competition 2025 results are available here, with more detailed ranking information accessible through those official results slides.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"080894f9-8f8e-4ab4-998a-4e94b3a7e032","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:28.291Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6c3d5193-b337-4ed8-847e-06453504fd2d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c198b284-b492-4f58-b935-bf37b140d6f8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a06de6cc1a7950537","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E672xEXQ1QGp2DacuvPaGF","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SAT Competition 2024 results main track winner Kissat CaDiCaL\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"The Results of SAT Competition 2024\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2024/downloads/satcomp24slides.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2024\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2024/results.html\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL, Gimsatul, IsaSAT and Kissat Entering the SAT Competition 2024\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFazekasFleuryFroleyksPollitt-SAT-Competition-2024-solvers.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Kissat triumphs in the SAT 2024 competition — English\",\"url\":\"https://news.vm.uni-freiburg.de/en/newsarchive/kissat-triumphs-in-the-sat-2024-competition\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Solver Etudes I | Hey There Buddo!\",\"url\":\"https://www.philipzucker.com/python_sat/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - arminbiere/kissat · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/kissat\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2024 Medals\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/sat24medals/\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL 2.2 System Description Artifact\",\"url\":\"https://zenodo.org/records/14923247\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - texmex76/kissat-cr\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/texmex76/kissat-cr\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2024/rules.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the SAT Competition 2024 main track results:\n\n## Main Track Winner\n\nThe main track UNSAT winner was kissat-sc2024, authored by Armin Biere, Tobias Faller, Katalin Fazekas, Mathias Fleury, Nils Froleyks, and Florian Pollitt, with a PAR-2 score of 2077.11 and 153 instances solved.\n\n## Overall Performance\n\nThe main track of the prestigious SAT 2024 competition was dominated by the latest version of the SAT solver Kissat, which secured first place in all disciplines and won three gold medals.\n\nRegarding CaDiCaL specifically, it also participated in the competition. Kissat is a \"keep it simple and clean bare metal SAT solver\" written in C, which is a port of CaDiCaL back to C with improved data structures, better scheduling of inprocessing and optimized algorithms and implementation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d7660390-62be-449c-84b9-2235181a973d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:28.293Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c198b284-b492-4f58-b935-bf37b140d6f8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"726072df-bada-4e60-b999-c4e7432260ca","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a06de6cc1a7950537","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011G11Um3nhsvUSN6uJ5qN8u","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Kissat 4.0 latest version 2025 Armin Biere release\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Release Release 4.0.1 · arminbiere/kissat\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/kissat/releases/tag/rel-4.0.1\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - arminbiere/kissat · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/kissat\"},{\"title\":\"Kissat Clause Reduction Version\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/artifact/10.4230/artifacts.24025\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · arminbiere/kissat\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/kissat/releases/\"},{\"title\":\"Learn to Unlearn\",\"url\":\"https://zenodo.org/records/15146408\"},{\"title\":\"kissat/README.md at master · arminbiere/kissat\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/kissat/blob/master/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"kissat/VERSION at master · arminbiere/kissat\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/kissat/blob/master/VERSION\"},{\"title\":\"Issues · arminbiere/kissat\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/kissat/issues\"},{\"title\":\"Learn to Unlearn\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.14\"},{\"title\":\"rustsat-kissat 0.3.3 - Docs.rs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/crate/rustsat-kissat/latest\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Kissat 4.0:\n\nThe latest version is 4.0.1, which was released by Armin Biere on September 12, 2024. This release included updates to the README to point to the 2024 system description, removed redundant lines in congruence closure, fixed proof chain generation for matching ITE, fixed getting size of watches for --compact, improved precision in congruence, fixed DIMACS writing to stdout with -o, and fixed reporting in congruence.\n\nYou can get more information about Kissat in the solver description for the SAT Competition 2024, authored by Armin Biere and colleagues.\n\nAdditionally, there is ongoing research work with Kissat. In 2025, Bernhard Gstrein, Florian Pollitt, André Schidler, Mathias Fleury, and Armin Biere published \"Learn to Unlearn\" at the 28th International Conference on Theory and Applications of Satisfiability Testing (SAT 2025), which involved a clause reduction version of Kissat.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"4fdc79e7-105d-459f-837f-bfcc77aa116a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:31.312Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"726072df-bada-4e60-b999-c4e7432260ca","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d2e890dc-a890-4fe7-9fd7-806b06759057","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a06de6cc1a7950537","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011ZxF2CajRMksjcUhhd85JE","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CaDiCaL 2.0 release 2024 2025 incremental SAT solver\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL 2.0 | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-65627-9_7\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - arminbiere/cadical: CaDiCaL SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL 2.0 CAV'24 Tool-Paper Artifact\",\"url\":\"https://zenodo.org/records/10943125\"},{\"title\":\"Available CAV Evaluation Artifact Reusable CAV Evaluation Artifact CaDiCaL 2.0\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFazekasFleuryFroleyksPollitt-CAV24.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL 2.0 | Computer Aided Verification\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1007/978-3-031-65627-9_7\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL 2.0 Armin Biere1,2(B) , Tobias Faller1 , Katalin Fazekas3\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/978-3-031-65627-9_7.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Solver in cadical - Rust\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/cadical/latest/cadical/struct.Solver.html\"},{\"title\":\"Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research 81 (2024) 989-1017\",\"url\":\"https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/download/16163/27111/42883\"},{\"title\":\"Revisiting DRUP-Based Interpolants with CaDiCaL 2.0 | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-90653-4_5\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · arminbiere/cadical\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/releases\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about CaDiCaL 2.0 and the incremental SAT solver:\n\n## CaDiCaL 2.0 Release\n\nCaDiCaL 2.0 was published by Armin Biere, Tobias Faller, Katalin Fazekas, Mathias Fleury, Nils Froleyks and Florian Pollitt at the 26th International Conference on Computer Aided Verification (CAV'24) in Lecture Notes in Computer Science volume 14681, pages 133-152, Springer 2024.\n\n## Features and Capabilities\n\nThe SAT solver CaDiCaL provides a rich feature set with a clean library interface. CaDiCaL has state-of-the-art performance both in a stand-alone as well as incremental setting.\n\n## Incremental Solving Support\n\nFor incremental solving, MiniSat has been the predominant choice, however, in recent years, CaDiCaL has begun to replace MiniSat in numerous applications, most prominently cvc5. The developers invested in increasing the feature set supported by CaDiCaL culminating in supporting \"user propagators\".\n\n## Recent Developments\n\nThe latest updates include a major IPASIR-UP increment with changes to the API syntax, including batched notification of assignments, support for clauses learned from propagators to be deleted, and added support to generate incremental proofs (LIDRUP) while using IPASIR-UP.\n\nThe solver is available on GitHub at https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e2211276-22fb-446f-b0a4-72d834f6e492","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:32.435Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d2e890dc-a890-4fe7-9fd7-806b06759057","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
