{"parentUuid":"96f6717c-ede5-4c98-a370-2a6e10f0d4a1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a06de6cc1a7950537","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DkTmE8hWLAjwmRFVpLwykR","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ParaFROST GPU SAT solver 2024 2025 status active\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - muhos/ParaFROST: A Parallel SAT Solver with GPU Accelerated Inprocessing\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/muhos/ParaFROST\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Solving with GPU Accelerated Inprocessing\",\"url\":\"https://www.win.tue.nl/~awijs/articles/parafrost_gpu.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GPU Acceleration of Bounded Model Checking with ParaFROST | Computer Aided Verification\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1007/978-3-030-81688-9_21\"},{\"title\":\"ParaFROST | A SAT Solver with GPU Accelerated Inprocessing | GPU library\",\"url\":\"https://kandi.openweaver.com/c++/muhos/ParaFROST\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Solving with GPU-Accelerated Inprocessing – GEARS: An NWO TOP funded research project\",\"url\":\"https://gears.win.tue.nl/software/parafrost/\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Certified SAT solving with GPU accelerated inprocessing\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/372857962_Certified_SAT_solving_with_GPU_accelerated_inprocessing\"},{\"title\":\"GPU Acceleration of Bounded Model Checking with ParaFROST | SpringerLink\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-81688-9_21\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Solving with GPU Accelerated Inprocessing - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7979176/\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Solving with GPU Accelerated Inprocessing | SpringerLink\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-72016-2_8\"},{\"title\":\"Certified SAT solving with GPU accelerated inprocessing | Formal Methods in System Design | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10703-023-00432-z\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about ParaFROST:\n\n## ParaFROST GPU SAT Solver Overview\n\nParaFROST is a parallel SAT solver with GPU accelerated inprocessing. It is capable of harnessing NVIDIA CUDA-enabled GPUs in applying modern simplification techniques in parallel.\n\n## Recent Activity (2023-2024)\n\nThe solver appears to be actively maintained with recent developments:\n\n- A 2024 publication in Formal Methods in System Design addressed certified SAT solving with GPU accelerated inprocessing, indicating ongoing research and improvements to the project.\n\n- The solver includes a novel algorithm to generate clausal proofs in parallel to validate all simplifications running on the GPU besides the CDCL search, giving high credibility to its use in critical applications such as model checkers.\n\n## Repository Status\n\nThe project is hosted on GitHub (muhos/ParaFROST), making the source code publicly available for development and community contributions.\n\nThe search results confirm that ParaFROST is an active research project with recent publications and developments in 2023-2024, particularly around certified SAT solving and proof generation capabilities.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"cb653989-238c-4273-bfba-a811dacaf20c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:43.003Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"96f6717c-ede5-4c98-a370-2a6e10f0d4a1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"1334484f-d7b4-4429-9f8a-3effb9deabe1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a06de6cc1a7950537","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013d7J5SQhYaBNUmY8WY7rku","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Painless SAT solver portfolio clause sharing 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"D-Painless: A Framework for Distributed Portfolio SAT Solving | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-90653-4_3\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) D-Painless: A Framework for Distributed Portfolio SAT Solving\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/391418351_D-Painless_A_Framework_for_Distributed_Portfolio_SAT_Solving\"},{\"title\":\"Parallel Clause Sharing Strategy Based on Graph Structure of SAT Problem\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol305-sat2024/LIPIcs.SAT.2024.17/LIPIcs.SAT.2024.17.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Streamlining Distributed SAT Solver Design Dominik Schreiber # Ñ\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/SchreiberRigiLupertiBiere-SAT25.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"MallobSat: Scalable SAT Solving by Clause Sharing\",\"url\":\"https://dominikschreiber.de/papers/2024-jair-mallobsat.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - lip6/painless: A framework to ease parallelization of sequential SAT solvers\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/lip6/painless\"},{\"title\":\"PaInleSS: a Framework for Parallel SAT Solving - Archive ouverte HAL\",\"url\":\"https://hal.science/hal-01540785v1\"},{\"title\":\"Unsatisfiability Proofs for Distributed Clause-Sharing SAT Solvers | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-30823-9_18\"},{\"title\":\"Validating Unsatisﬁability Results of Clause Sharing Parallel SAT Solvers\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.utexas.edu/~marijn/publications/pos14.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Producing Proofs of Unsatisfiability with Distributed Clause-Sharing SAT Solvers | Journal of Automated Reasoning | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10817-025-09725-w\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Painless SAT solver portfolio clause sharing in 2024-2025:\n\n## Key Developments\n\nD-Painless is a new extension of the Painless framework to include distributed portfolio strategy and clause sharing, aimed at broadening Painless's functionality for more effective distributed SAT solving methodologies. The new architecture was assessed using 400 instances from the SAT'2024 competition, each with a timeout limit of 500 seconds.\n\n## Portfolio Strategy and Clause Sharing\n\nThe portfolio strategy, combined with clause sharing, has emerged as the leading approach for both local and distributed parallelization on CPUs. While solver diversification remains beneficial, its impact becomes secondary compared to the collaborative learning achieved through clause sharing.\n\n## Recent Advances (2024-2025)\n\nRecent work has focused on improving how clauses are shared in portfolio solvers. P-KISSAT, based on the painless framework, dynamically varies the criterion for sharing learnt clauses depending on the number of clauses generated by the producer of clauses.\n\nAdditionally, distributed clause-sharing SAT solvers can solve challenging problems hundreds of times faster than sequential SAT solvers by sharing derived information among multiple sequential solvers. However, distributed solvers have not been able to produce proofs of unsatisfiability in a scalable manner, which limits their use in critical applications. Recent work presents a method to produce unsatisfiability proofs for distributed SAT solvers by combining the partial proofs produced by each sequential solver into a single, linear proof.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"1468e1b7-cbd4-486c-98b0-66983ee681a5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:43.136Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1334484f-d7b4-4429-9f8a-3effb9deabe1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"5860e8c1-c47c-451b-992f-c78d8e300b02","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a06de6cc1a7950537","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dfej4FaHpj1yg6AK5QBZ1q","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"IPASIR-UP user propagator CaDiCaL 2025 learner API\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"cadical/NEWS.md at master · arminbiere/cadical\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/blob/master/NEWS.md\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL Katalin Fazekas # TU Wien, Austria\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol271-sat2023/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research 81 (2024) 989-1017\",\"url\":\"https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/download/16163/27111/42883\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL 2.0 Armin Biere1,2(B) , Tobias Faller1 , Katalin Fazekas3\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/978-3-031-65627-9_7.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL Katalin Fazekas # TU Wien, Vienna, Austria\",\"url\":\"https://cs.stanford.edu/~niemetz/publications/2023/FazekasNPKSB-SAT23.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · arminbiere/cadical\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/releases\"},{\"title\":\"Supplementary material of submission \\\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL\\\"\",\"url\":\"https://zenodo.org/records/8003683\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL\",\"url\":\"https://www-cs.stanford.edu/~niemetz/talks/Niemetz-SMT23.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL A CaDiCaL Integration into CDCL(T )\",\"url\":\"https://cs.stanford.edu/~niemetz/talks/Niemetz-CENTAUR23.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about IPASIR-UP user propagator in CaDiCaL and its learner API:\n\n## IPASIR-UP Overview\n\nIPASIR-UP is an interface for User Propagators for CDCL. The interface allows inspecting and influencing the internal behaviour of CDCL SAT solvers, capturing essential functionalities for more fine-grained interaction with the SAT solver than provided via the standard IPASIR interface.\n\n## CaDiCaL 2025 Updates\n\nThere was a major IPASIR-UP increment with changes that affect the syntax of the API, including batched notification of assignments into arrays instead of fixed flags, allowing clauses learned from the propagator to be deleted with new parameters, and added support to generate incremental proofs (LIDRUP) while using IPASIR-UP.\n\n## Learner API\n\nThe dynamic API interacts and controls the solver during search, with the solver providing dynamic access to clauses learned during conflict analysis to connected Learner instances.\n\n## Key Callback Functions\n\nIPASIR-UP provides callbacks (with prefix \"cb_\") in five states to interact with the external propagator, and the propagator is notified about changes to the trail. The main functions include `cb_propagate`, `cb_add_reason_clause_lit`, `cb_decide`, and `cb_add_external_clause_lit` for propagations, explanations, decisions, and adding lemmas respectively.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"9e348a59-aee9-47be-9893-bc3703ccdf40","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:43.235Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5860e8c1-c47c-451b-992f-c78d8e300b02","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"60505fab-b00f-4907-9fbd-150dd89014f8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a06de6cc1a7950537","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tjr8i8htRUvQiDun1g9aZz","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"MallobSat parallel SAT solver KIT 2025 portfolio scaling\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"KIT - SAtRes - MallobSat scores 1st in SAT Competition\",\"url\":\"https://satres.kikit.kit.edu/news/2025-08-15-satcomp/\"},{\"title\":\"Streamlining Distributed SAT Solver Design - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol341-sat2025/html/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.27/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.27.html\"},{\"title\":\"From Scalable SAT to MaxSAT: Massively Parallel Solution Improving Search\",\"url\":\"https://satres.kikit.kit.edu/papers/2025-socs-distributed-maxsat.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - domschrei/mallob: Malleable Load Balancer. Massively Parallel Logic Backend. Award-winning SAT solving for the cloud.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/domschrei/mallob\"},{\"title\":\"MallobSat naps in the SAT Competition 2025 Dominik Schreiber\",\"url\":\"https://satres.kikit.kit.edu/papers/2025-mallob-naps.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"HordeSat: A Massively Parallel Portfolio SAT Solver | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/276296424_HordeSat_A_Massively_Parallel_Portfolio_SAT_Solver\"},{\"title\":\"D-Painless: A Framework for Distributed Portfolio SAT Solving | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-90653-4_3\"},{\"title\":\"MallobSat: Scalable SAT Solving by Clause Sharing - SAtRes\",\"url\":\"https://satres.kikit.kit.edu/papers/2024-jair-mallobsat.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"MallobSat: Scalable SAT Solving by Clause Sharing\",\"url\":\"https://dominikschreiber.de/papers/2024-jair-mallobsat.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"MallobSat: Scalable SAT Solving by Clause Sharing | Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research\",\"url\":\"https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/view/15827\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's information about MallobSat, the parallel SAT solver from KIT, regarding its 2025 portfolio scaling:\n\n## Key Findings on MallobSat's 2025 Portfolio Approach\n\nMallobSat's 2025 submission features a simplified and streamlined parallel solver design that employs minimal solver diversification (random seeds and variable phases only) and sequential preprocessors followed by parallel search-only Kissat threads plus a few YalSAT stochastic local search threads.\n\n### Portfolio Scaling Strategy\n\nThis setup departs from the prevalent notion of a \"diverse portfolio\" and is closer to a uniform parallel CDCL procedure, powered by clause sharing. The approach is informally called \"NAPS\" — \"not a portfolio solver!\"\n\nThe 2025 version replaces redundant pre- and inprocessing at all threads with single-core preprocessing that runs next to the parallel search, removes LBD values from the clause-sharing operation, and slims down solver diversification. Experimental evaluations on up to 3072 cores confirm that these measures improve performance while drastically simplifying the SAT solving program.\n\n### 2025 Competition Results\n\n2025 marks the first year where MallobSat was able to win the SAT competition's shared-memory parallel main track (64 threads). All configurations of MallobSat show consistent performance improvements up to the largest scale considered (3072 cores).\n\nThis represents a significant shift toward simplification and efficiency in distributed SAT solving, moving away from traditional portfolio approaches.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"50fc28aa-cc23-4c5c-a91b-14543fee67d3","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:44.170Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"60505fab-b00f-4907-9fbd-150dd89014f8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
