{"parentUuid":"f010e9a6-e8f9-4c05-8358-83f4734747fc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a06de6cc1a7950537","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012yP9SBL9JZquyodQCFUpBu","type":"tool_result","content":"# SAT Competition Results Summary\n\n## Main Track (Sequential) - Top 5\n\n1. **VBS** - Score: 1681.3, Solved: 347\n2. **kissat-sc2024** - Score: 2788.13, Solved: 306\n3. **Kissat_MAB-DC** - Score: 3435.23, Solved: 290\n4. **hKis-bva** - Score: 3461.15, Solved: 285\n5. **BreakID-Kissat** - Score: 3461.77, Solved: 284\n\n**Medals:** Gold: VBS, Silver: kissat-sc2024, Bronze: Kissat_MAB-DC\n\n## Parallel Track - Top 5\n\n1. **VBS** - Score: 932.72, Solved: 370\n2. **saoudi-painless-par2** - Score: 1397.76, Solved: 353\n3. **saoudi-painless-par1** - Score: 1418.19, Solved: 353\n4. **tchinda-prs-pakisinc** - Score: 1507.7, Solved: 349\n5. **djamegni-sbvaprspakisinc** - Score: 1572.25, Solved: 348\n\n**Medals:** Gold: VBS, Silver: saoudi-painless-par2, Bronze: saoudi-painless-par1\n\n## Incremental Track\n\nNo incremental track results appear in the provided content."}]},"uuid":"f052ba8e-e293-42e7-9fc2-0a5717333fca","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:54.203Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f010e9a6-e8f9-4c05-8358-83f4734747fc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"921becc2-44c3-47c3-95f6-b9b17b3d3f03","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a06de6cc1a7950537","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LqZaxqc1j3Jxmb1LHGB8oo","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SAT solver long running 1 hour industrial benchmark CDCL performance\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"(PDF) Boosting the Performance of CDCL-Based SAT Solvers by Exploiting Backbones and Backdoors\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/363062434_Boosting_the_Performance_of_CDCL-Based_SAT_Solvers_by_Exploiting_Backbones_and_Backdoors\"},{\"title\":\"Improving Performance of CDCL SAT Solvers by ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/1462513\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - RobertObkircher/sat-solver: CDCL SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/RobertObkircher/sat-solver\"},{\"title\":\"Towards Improving the Resource Usage of SAT solvers\",\"url\":\"https://iccl.inf.tu-dresden.de/w/images/0/0a/Manthey:10:POS.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"JOURNAL OF LATEX CLASS FILES, VOL. 18, NO. 9, SEPTEMBER 2020 1\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2501.14740\"},{\"title\":\"[1706.08611] Relating Complexity-theoretic Parameters with SAT Solver Performance\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.08611\"},{\"title\":\"Boosting the Performance of CDCL-Based SAT Solvers by Exploiting Backbones and Backdoors\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/1999-4893/15/9/302\"},{\"title\":\"1 On The Unreasonable Eﬀectiveness of SAT Solvers\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.rice.edu/~vardi/papers/SATSolvers21.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Proceedings of SAT COMPETITION 2020 Solver and Benchmark Descriptions\",\"url\":\"https://tuhat.helsinki.fi/ws/files/142452772/sc2020_proceedings.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Cube and Conquer: Guiding CDCL SAT Solvers by Lookaheads ⋆\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.utexas.edu/~marijn/publications/cube.pdf\"}]\n\nI found relevant research results for your query on SAT solvers with CDCL performance benchmarks. Here's what the search returned:\n\n## Key Research Areas\n\nModifying the VSIDS heuristic in CDCL solvers to exploit backbones and backdoors improves performance, with new solvers solving more industrial SAT instances than winning CDCL SAT solvers in 2020 and 2021 SAT competitions.\n\nResearch has been conducted to explain the efficiency of conflict-driven clause-learning (CDCL) SAT solvers on large industrial Boolean instances, with large-scale empirical evaluation of CDCL SAT solver performance on nearly 7000 industrial and crafted formulas.\n\n## Industrial Benchmark Studies\n\nVariants of CDCL solvers were evaluated on 32 industrial families from 2002 to 2021 SAT competitions.\n\nResearch on SAT solver performance on industrial datapath circuits included timeouts of 1 hour in their test settings.\n\n## Performance Analysis\n\nPerformance results have been studied comparing modified CDCL SAT solvers with state-of-the-art CDCL SAT solvers on industrial benchmarks.\n\nThe search results cover research on CDCL solver optimizations, industrial benchmark evaluations, and structural parameters that influence solver performance, though not all results specifically focus on 1-hour long-running benchmarks.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"fa710c8c-1ccb-4919-a4aa-da1dd101ae6e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:55.204Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"921becc2-44c3-47c3-95f6-b9b17b3d3f03","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"32a73503-f045-489e-82ec-a1db5db0dfae","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a06de6cc1a7950537","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PVrUtzszmDBgG9XS4QuXih","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT vs SAT solver hybrid approach OR-Tools combinatorial\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"📈 #76 Optimizing with Google OR-Tools: strategies and insights from three years of real-world experience\",\"url\":\"https://www.feasible.club/p/76-optimizing-with-google-or-tools\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SAT solver vs. CP solver\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/Pa5eQUoLnow\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"SAT solver - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SAT_solver\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Constraint Programming Solver | google/or-tools | DeepWiki\",\"url\":\"https://deepwiki.com/google/or-tools/4.1-cp-sat-constraint-programming-solver\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the CP-SAT vs SAT solver hybrid approach in OR-Tools:\n\n## Overview\n\nThe CP-SAT solver is a powerful hybrid solver combining techniques from constraint programming, SAT solving, and mixed-integer programming. This hybrid approach enables efficient solutions for constraint satisfaction and optimization problems across various domains.\n\n## How the Hybrid Approach Works\n\nCP-SAT essentially translates CP constraints into a SAT formula (incrementally), and then uses a SAT solver to find a solution or prove unsatisfiability. The integration uses a technique called Lazy Clause Generation (LCG):\n\nPropagation (CP side) shrinks variable domains by local reasoning (all-different, cumulative, bounds …). Conflict-Driven Clause Learning (SAT side) analyzes a failure, extracts a nogood clause that cuts off all equivalent failing assignments, and backjumps. Every propagator can explain why it shrank a domain; that explanation is pushed into the SAT core as a clause. Next time a similar partial assignment appears, the SAT engine prunes it before CP work is repeated.\n\n## Performance Benefits\n\nThis hybrid approach often gives CP-SAT one to two orders of magnitude fewer search nodes than plain CP and faster backjumps than plain SAT. It's particularly effective for hard combinatorial optimization.\n\n## Technical Architecture\n\nAt its core is a modern CDCL (Conflict-Driven Clause Learning) SAT solver with specialized components for handling integer variables, constraints, and optimization objectives.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e7899cb6-0359-4959-9276-24487a6eb301","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:55.281Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"32a73503-f045-489e-82ec-a1db5db0dfae","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f00fe09f-0ec7-49f6-9c44-3d41eaa0dee7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a06de6cc1a7950537","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019GK28ZqY5m7sCtfqpjTAg3","type":"tool_result","content":"# SAT Competition 2025 Results\n\nBased on the provided content, here's what is documented:\n\n**Main Parallel Track (64 threads):**\nMallobSat won first place, scoring the best on unsatisfiable instances. The margin was narrow, with only \"3% to Painless-PRS-Kissat in terms of the PAR-2 evaluation metric.\" Painless-PRS-Kissat by Saoudi et al. came second, performing better on satisfiable instances.\n\n**Cloud Track:**\nThe article notes that \"This year's competition did not feature a distributed 'Cloud' track (1600 threads),\" so no results are available for 2025. However, the text mentions that MallobSat had \"consistently scored the best since 2020\" in previous years' cloud competitions.\n\n**Sequential and Incremental Tracks:**\nThe document does not provide information about winners in sequential or incremental tracks.\n\nThe article emphasizes that MallobSat's 2025 victory marked \"the first year where our system was able to win the SAT competition's shared-memory parallel main track,\" representing a notable achievement despite the absence of the cloud competition category."}]},"uuid":"481ef14e-1a0a-4158-8b84-a4fa694334cf","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:57.867Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f00fe09f-0ec7-49f6-9c44-3d41eaa0dee7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
